# LINE ENDINGS ARE PINNED FOR MARKDOWN, and the reason is a test.
#
# `crates/tacet-cli/README.md` is GENERATED from the root README by
# `crates/tacet-cli/tests/readme_mirror.rs`, and the generated header is a Rust
# string literal — always LF. On a Windows checkout with git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` the committed files arrive with CRLF, so the mirror and
# the freshly generated text differed by five bytes and the test failed on
# windows-latest alone. Pinning the checkout is the root fix; the test also
# normalises, because a claim about what two documents SAY should not rest on a
# git setting.
*.md text eol=lf
